      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start, really captures the energy. but i want to dig deeper into how he justifies the downsides. like, people are gonna scream that this will cause massive inflation and destroy the manufacturing sector because of supply chain issues. how does he address those specific criticisms in the speech? i want him to pivot from the \"emotional appeal\" to a logical-sounding argument that explains why those economic costs are actually a necessary and even beneficial sacrifice for long-term stability.",
