      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "(Elias pauses, letting the murmurs of the crowd subside, before responding)\n\n\"Now, I know some of you think that closing our borders will lead to a chain reaction of devastating economic consequences – that unfettered competition and cheaper goods will crush our families, that we'll be abandoned to the whims of international markets. But the truth is, our current economic system isn't designed to serve the people of this nation; it's a relic of a bygone era, fueling inequality and fostering dependency on cheap imports. The automation of manufacturing is not a threat – it's a catalyst. And by giving our industries the freedom to adapt, to innovate in response to shifting global power dynamics, we'll be creating jobs that can't be outsourced, that won't be swallowed up by global giants. The 'inflation' you speak of is an illusion, a reset – a necessary rebalancing of our economy, as we shed the weight of a system that's served to enrich the 1% at our expense. The benefits won't be immediate, but they will be enduring, as we build an American economy that truly serves its own interests – a self-sustaining engine, driven by innovation, not speculation, and responsive to the",
